#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129268 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128845 :question/id #uuid "043cc93d-1eae-5640-a109-9acbe7a34f92" :question/math-academy-id "e-11471" :question/problem "If the solid region $R$ is given by \n\n$$\nR = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\, : \\, (x-1)^2 + y^2 \\leq 1, \\: -2 \\leq z \\leq 4-y \\right\\},\n$$\n\nthen express the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2} \\: \\textrm{d}V\n$$\n\nas an equivalent integral in cylindrical polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iiint\\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\, \\mathrm{d}V = \n\\iiint\\limits_{\\Delta} \\, f(r \\cos\\theta, r\\sin\\theta, z) \\:  r \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\, \\mathrm{d}r \\, \\mathrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nIf $(r, \\theta, z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx = r\\cos\\theta, \\qquad\ny = r\\sin\\theta, \\qquad \nz = z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/a5/a551e379767395a2422f690a66fc38defab64cff03c752c0c9a5a0748561d2f7.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $1$ whose axis passes through the point $(1,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z = -2,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z = 4 - y = 4 - r\\sin{\\theta}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's write the equation $(x-1)^2 + y^2 = 1$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1)}^{2}+{(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1+{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire circle, we must have $r = 2\\cos{\\theta}.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\Delta = \\left\\{ (r,\\theta,z) \\, : \\, 0 \\leq r \\leq 2\\cos{\\theta}, \\: -\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\leq \\theta \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\: -2 \\leq z \\leq 4-r\\sin{\\theta} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\int }_{-2}^{4-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aea71b56-dd09-564e-a2bf-5606233e2819" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537081 :question-generator/id #uuid "176ad11d-77c9-58f9-aaa7-c4d7d3927260" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186129268.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129517 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8677d1f9-393e-54ba-86b0-46dcf9a4cbfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{π}^{2π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{-6 sin ⁡ θ}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2 + r 2}r 3 cos ⁡ θ sin ⁡ θdzdrdθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126603} {:answer/id #uuid "0f8d8993-e95e-5762-b88f-6db309b818d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{π}^{2π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{3}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2 + r}r 3 cos ⁡ θ sin ⁡ θdzdrdθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126604} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa7b7c9-1d88-53f2-9f82-f9e192924e23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{π}^{2π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{6 cos ⁡ θ}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2 + r 2}r 3 cos ⁡ θ sin ⁡ θ